		summary = "**The Sound and the Fury** is a novel by the American author [[William Faulkner]], published in 1929. Faulkner's fourth novel, it is the second to be set in Yoknapatawpha County and the first featuring the Compson family, both of which would reappear in his later fiction. The novel's highly experimental style, including its use of [[Stream of consciousness|stream of consciousness]] and multiple different unreliable narrators, are hallmarks of [[Literary modernism|modernist literature]]. Its bleak and candid portrait of Southern life in the early 20th century is paradigmatic of the Southern Gothic genre.",
